<title>USA: Colo. 428 MW coal-fired unit to shut over weekend.</title>
<headline>Colo. 428 MW coal-fired unit to shut over weekend.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 428 megawatt (MW) unit at the Craig power plant in Colorado will be shut Friday night for maintenance and is expected to restart Monday morning, a spokesman for Tri-State Generation and Transmission Association said Friday.</p>
<p>The coal-fired plant also has a second 428 MW unit and another with a 408 MW capacity.</p>
<p>Besides Tri-State, the owners of the Craig station are Public Service Co of Colorado, PacifiCorp, the Salt River Project and the Platte River Authority.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
